course: dictionary
lesson: 7554
title: Prehensile: a body part that grips
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some animals use their bodies in clever ways. A «prehensile» body part can grip, hold or wrap around things. Prehensile is an adjective, so it describes a body part such as a tail, foot, trunk or lip.
explain: Look at the words near it: «Spider monkeys have a prehensile, gripping tail.» The word gripping sits right beside prehensile, so it is a clue. A tail that grips is a tail that can hold on to branches.
explain: Now try your meaning in the sentence. «Spider monkeys have a gripping tail that can hold on to branches.» It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning. Prehensile and gripping mean nearly the same thing here.
explain: Science lessons use the word when they study adaptations, which are features that help an animal survive. A chameleon, a seahorse and a possum can all hang on with a prehensile tail. An elephant's trunk is prehensile too, and human hands, with their thumbs, are said to be prehensile.
fact: Prehensile means able to grip, hold or wrap around things.
fact: Prehensile is used about body parts such as a tail, foot, trunk or lip.
fact: «Gripping» is a clue word: a prehensile tail is a gripping tail.
fact: Many monkeys of Central and South America have a prehensile tail, but no African or Asian monkeys have one.
fact: A spider monkey's prehensile tail has bare, ridged skin under the tip.
exercise: «Spider monkeys have a prehensile, gripping tail.» What does prehensile mean? | Long and furry | Very colourful | Able to swim fast | *Able to grip and hold on
exercise: Which body part does a science lesson call prehensile because it can grip? | A rabbit's ear | *An elephant's trunk | A cow's horn
exercise: «Many monkeys of Central and South America have a gripping, or prehensile, tail.» Which monkeys have prehensile tails? | Monkeys of Asia | Monkeys of Africa | *Monkeys of Central and South America
test: Which word in «a prehensile, gripping tail» is closest in meaning to prehensile? | ridged | *gripping | under | bare
test: Which animal in the science lessons can hang on to plants with a prehensile tail? | *A seahorse | A giraffe | A cow
exam: Ella says a prehensile tail is just a long tail. What is the best answer? | *A tail that can grip, hold or wrap around things | A tail that only helps an animal swim | Any tail that is long
